// The hyphenation patterns documents are hyphenated with: TeX's, from the
// hyph-utf8 package (the tex-hyphen repository), by Liang's algorithm
// (crates/text/src/hyphen.rs), for English (US and UK), German, French,
// Spanish, Norwegian (Bokmål and Nynorsk), Swedish, Russian and Greek
// (project owner, 2026-10-22, review pysc65hp).
//
// They aren't committed: `cargo run -p fetch-fonts` downloads them into
// hyphenation/, beside the fonts, from a pinned commit, and checks each
// against its hash. CI does the same. They ship as they come, unmodified,
// which every licence below allows, the LPPL included, and each with the
// TeX file whose header holds its copyright and licence (`notices`). The
// app reads a language's files the first time text in it is hyphenated.
//
// Each language has the tags it hyphenates;
// text in a language with no tag here takes its base language's, so
// en-CA hyphenates as en (crates/text, Hyphenation::get). `left` and
// `right` are the fewest letters a break leaves before and after it, as
// each file's header gives them for typesetting.
